  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Data analysis and Methodology <a name = 'h4'><a>"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Data Reduction <a name = 'h41'><a>"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "We began our analysis by selecting only those stars which seemed to be the cluster members.\n",
    "To obtain these possible members, we selected stars based on the following\n",
    "criteria:\n",
    "1) Proper motion of the star consistent with the proper motion of the cluster.\n",
    "2) Consistent with the selection based on the membership probabilities.\n",
    "3) Location in the color-magnitude diagram (CMD) consistent with the CMD of the cluster."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Only stars that met the mentioned criteria were considered probable members of the cluster.\n",
    "- These criteria were applied to all stars located within a radius extending up to five times the tidal radius ($r_{t}$) of the cluster.\n",
    "- Stars positioned between $r_{t}$ and $5r_{t}$ from the center of the cluster were identified as **extra-tidal candidates** for further analysis.\n",
    "- For this study, the adopted value of $r_{t}$ is 6.6 arcmin. "
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Proper Motion Selection <a name = 'h42'><a>"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Proper Motion\n",
    "It is the apparent angular motion of a star across the sky with respect to more distant stars.\n",
    "<img src=\"https://www.astronomy.ohio-state.edu/pogge.1/Ast162/Unit1/Images/space.gif\" width=\"40%\">\n",
    "---\n",
    "Representation of pmra ($\\mu_{\\alpha} \\cos {\\delta}$) and pmdec ($\\mu_{\\delta}$) on a celestial sphere:\n",
    "<img src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/08/Components_of_proper_motion.svg/375px-Components_of_proper_motion.svg.png\" width=\"20%\">\n",
    "\n",
    "For **NGC 4147**:  \n",
    "1) Right Ascension (RA): 182.5263°  \n",
    "2) Declination (Dec): 18.542°\n",
    "\n",
    "3) Mean Proper Motion:\n",
    "  - $\\overline{\\mu_{\\alpha} \\cos\\delta} = -1.71$ mas yr$^{-1}$  \n",
    "  - $\\overline{\\mu_{\\delta}} = -2.08$ mas yr$^{-1}$\n",
    "\n",
    "4) Proper Motion Uncertainties:  \n",
    "  - $\\sigma_{\\mu_{\\alpha} \\cos\\delta} = 0.21$ mas yr$^{-1}$  \n",
    "  - $\\sigma_{\\mu_{\\delta}} = 0.19$ mas yr$^{-1}$\n",
    "\n",
    "These values are taken from the literature."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Now, in order to obtain likely cluster members, we cut the sample at $PM \\pm 3\\sigma$ to only select stars as our cluster members: \n",
    "  \n",
    "$$\n",
    "\\sqrt{\\left(\\mu_{\\alpha}\\cos\\delta - \\overline{\\mu_{\\alpha}\\cos\\delta}\\right)^2 + \\left(\\mu_{\\delta} - \\overline{\\mu_{\\delta}}\\right)^2} < 3\\sqrt{\\sigma_{\\mu_{\\alpha}\\cos\\delta}^2 + \\sigma_{\\mu_{\\delta}}^2}\n",
    "$$"
   ]
  },
