   "source": [
    "### Performing Isochrone fitting for estimating the age, metallicity and selecting the likely extra-tidal candidates of the Cluster <a name = 'h45'><a>"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### What are stellar isochrones?\n",
    "\n",
    "In stellar evolution, an isochrone is a curve on the Hertzsprung-Russell diagram, representing a population of stars of the same age but with different mass.\n",
    "\n",
    "Isochrone fitting involves comparing theoretical stellar evolution tracks with observed CMDs. We selected 6 isochrone models from PARSEC database each with varying:\n",
    "- **Age** (in log(Age/yr))\n",
    "- **Metallicity** ([Fe/H] in dex)\n",
    "\n",
    "Each isochrone represents a population of stars with specific age and chemical composition. PARSEC models provide apparent magnitudes in Gaia $G$, $G_{BP}$, and $G_{RP}$ bands, which will be further corrected for extinction and distance modulus.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Fitting Methodology\n",
    "<a id=\"fitting-methodology\"></a>\n",
    "\n",
    "In the observed Color-Magnitude Diagram (CMD), a small interval in $G_{\\text{mag}}$ typically corresponds to a range of $(G_{\\rm BP} - G_{\\rm RP})$ values. To capture the underlying stellar sequence, we perform interpolation by dividing the $G_{\\text{mag}}$ axis (y-axis) into rectangular bins of size 0.1 mag, and for each such bin, we create a $(G_{\\rm BP} - G_{\\rm RP})$ bin [Layden et al. 2005](https://doi.org/10.1086/444407).\n",
    "\n",
    "Before this binning process, we exclude horizontal branch stars, blue stragglers, and field stars from the CMD. For a given small range of $G_{\\text{mag}}$, there are typically many data points with varying $(G_{\\rm BP} - G_{\\rm RP})$ values. The interpolation is performed using the following procedure:\n",
    "\n",
    "#### Interpolation Procedure\n",
    "\n",
    "1. For a given small range of $G_{\\text{mag}}$, create a bin of all $(G_{\\rm BP} - G_{\\rm RP})$ (x-axis) values.\n",
    "2. Compute the **mean** ($\\mu$) and **standard deviation** ($\\sigma$) of this bin.\n",
    "3. Create a refined bin by selecting only those $(G_{\\rm BP} - G_{\\rm RP})$ values that lie within the range $[\\mu - \\sigma,\\, \\mu + \\sigma]$.\n",
    "4. Compute the **median** of the $(G_{\\rm BP} - G_{\\rm RP})$ values in this refined bin.\n",
    "5. Repeat steps 2 and 3 iteratively:\n",
    "    - After each iteration, calculate the difference between the updated and previous mean.\n",
    "    - Continue until the change in mean is **less than 0.005**.\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "### Best Fit Isochrone Selection\n",
    "<a id=\"best-isochrone\"></a>\n",
    "\n",
    "To determine the best fit to the interpolated CMD:\n",
    "\n",
    "- For each point $i$ in the interpolated CMD, compute the **difference along the x-axis** between this point and the nearest point on a given isochrone.\n",
    "- Calculate the **absolute value** of this difference and average it over all points.\n",
    "- Repeat the above steps for all isochrones with different ages and metallicities.\n",
    "- The isochrone that yields the **lowest mean absolute error** is considered the best fit to the interpolated CMD and the observed diagram.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 20,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "\n",
      "Final count of extra-tidal stars within ±0.1 mag of best-fit isochrone: 9\n",
      "\n",
      "Best-Fit Isochrone:\n",
      "File     : C:\\Users\\hp\\Downloads\\output13e91.8\\output13e91.8.dat\n",
      "[Fe/H]   : -1.80\n",
      "Age      : 1.30e+10 yr\n",
      "MAE      : 0.0589\n"
     ]
    },
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "\n",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 600x600 with 1 Axes>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "from scipy.spatial import cKDTree\n",
    "\n",
    "# ========== Constants ==========\n",
    "Rg, Rbp, Rrp = 2.685, 3.268, 2.002\n",
    "Ebv = 0.02\n",
    "mag_limit_min, mag_limit_max = 12, 22\n",
    "color_limit_min, color_limit_max = 0.0, 2.2\n",
    "fixed_DM = 16.49 #Harris Catalog\n",
    "bin_height = 0.1\n",
    "convergence_eps = 0.005\n",
    "color_tol = 0.1\n",
    "mag_tol = 0.1\n",
    "\n",
    "# ========== Load Cluster Data ==========\n",
    "cluster_df = pd.read_csv(\"cluster_stars_filtered.csv\").dropna(subset=[\"bp_rp\", \"phot_g_mean_mag\"])\n",
    "cluster_df[\"bp_rp_0\"] = cluster_df[\"bp_rp\"] - (Rbp - Rrp) * Ebv\n",
    "cluster_df[\"G0\"] = cluster_df[\"phot_g_mean_mag\"] - Rg * Ebv\n",
    "\n",
    "# Filter CMD: Remove Horizontal Branch, Blue Stragglers\n",
    "filtered_df = cluster_df[(cluster_df[\"G0\"] > 15) & (cluster_df[\"G0\"] < 20.5)]\n",
    "filtered_df = filtered_df[(filtered_df[\"bp_rp_0\"] > color_limit_min) & (filtered_df[\"bp_rp_0\"] < color_limit_max)]\n",
    "\n",
    "# ========== Load and Process Extra-Tidal Data ==========\n",
    "extra_df = pd.read_csv(\"extra-tidal_filtered.csv\").dropna(subset=[\"bp_rp\", \"phot_g_mean_mag\"])\n",
    "extra_df[\"bp_rp_0\"] = extra_df[\"bp_rp\"] - (Rbp - Rrp) * Ebv\n",
    "extra_df[\"G0\"] = extra_df[\"phot_g_mean_mag\"] - Rg * Ebv\n",
    "\n",
    "# ========== Interpolate CMD ==========\n",
    "interpolated_cmd = []\n",
    "g_vals = filtered_df[\"G0\"].values\n",
    "c_vals = filtered_df[\"bp_rp_0\"].values\n",
    "bins = np.arange(g_vals.min(), g_vals.max(), bin_height)\n",
    "\n",
    "for g_min in bins:\n",
    "    g_max = g_min + bin_height\n",
    "    mask = (g_vals >= g_min) & (g_vals < g_max)\n",
    "    color_bin = c_vals[mask]\n",
    "    if len(color_bin) < 5:\n",
    "        continue\n",
    "\n",
    "    mu_old = np.mean(color_bin)\n",
    "    sigma_old = np.std(color_bin)\n",
    "\n",
    "    while True:\n",
    "        sub_bin = color_bin[(color_bin > mu_old - sigma_old) & (color_bin < mu_old + sigma_old)]\n",
    "        if len(sub_bin) < 3:\n",
    "            break\n",
    "        mu_new = np.mean(sub_bin)\n",
    "        if abs(mu_new - mu_old) < convergence_eps:\n",
    "            break\n",
    "        mu_old = mu_new\n",
    "        sigma_old = np.std(sub_bin)\n",
    "\n",
    "    median_val = np.median(sub_bin)\n",
    "    interpolated_cmd.append([(g_min + g_max) / 2, median_val])\n",
    "\n",
    "interpolated_cmd = np.array(interpolated_cmd)\n",
    "interp_G0 = interpolated_cmd[:, 0]\n",
    "interp_color = interpolated_cmd[:, 1]\n",
    "\n",
    "# ========== Isochrone File Setup ==========\n",
    "column_names = [\n",
    "    \"Zini\", \"MH\", \"logAge\", \"Mini\", \"int_IMF\", \"Mass\", \"logL\", \"logTe\", \"logg\", \"label\",\n",
    "    \"McoreTP\", \"C_O\", \"period0\", \"period1\", \"period2\", \"period3\", \"period4\", \"pmode\",\n",
    "    \"Mloss\", \"tau1m\", \"X\", \"Y\", \"Xc\", \"Xn\", \"Xo\", \"Cexcess\", \"Z\", \"mbolmag\",\n",
    "    \"Gmag\", \"G_BPmag\", \"G_RPmag\"\n",
    "]\n",
    "\n",
    "isochrone_files = [\n",
    "    r\"C:\\Users\\hp\\Downloads\\output11e91.75dat\\output11e91.75dat.dat\",\n",
    "    r\"C:\\Users\\hp\\Downloads\\output11e91.78.dat\\output11e91.78.dat\",\n",
    "    r\"C:\\Users\\hp\\Downloads\\output11e91.8.dat\\output11e91.8.dat\",\n",
    "    r\"C:\\Users\\hp\\Downloads\\output12e91.8.dat\\output12e91.8.dat\",\n",
    "    r\"C:\\Users\\hp\\Downloads\\output10e91.8.dat\\output10e91.8.dat\",\n",
    "    r\"C:\\Users\\hp\\Downloads\\output13e91.8\\output13e91.8.dat\"\n",
    "]\n",
    "\n",
    "fit_results = []\n",
    "\n",
    "# ========== Fit Isochrones ==========\n",
    "for path in isochrone_files:\n",
    "    iso = pd.read_csv(path, sep=r\"\\s+\", header=None, names=column_names, comment=\"#\")\n",
    "    iso[\"bp_rp_0\"] = (iso[\"G_BPmag\"] - iso[\"G_RPmag\"]) - (Rbp - Rrp) * Ebv\n",
    "    iso[\"G0\"] = iso[\"Gmag\"] - Rg * Ebv + fixed_DM\n",
    "\n",
    "    valid = (iso[\"G0\"] > mag_limit_min) & (iso[\"G0\"] < mag_limit_max)\n",
    "#     not_HB = ~((iso[\"bp_rp_0\"] < 0.5) & (iso[\"G0\"] < 18.0))\n",
    "#     not_BS = ~((iso[\"bp_rp_0\"] < 0.3) & (iso[\"G0\"] < 19.0))\n",
    "#     valid = valid & not_HB & not_BS\n",
    "\n",
    "    if valid.sum() < 5:\n",
    "        continue\n",
    "\n",
    "    iso_color = iso.loc[valid, \"bp_rp_0\"].values\n",
    "    iso_mag = iso.loc[valid, \"G0\"].values\n",
    "\n",
    "    tree = cKDTree(np.column_stack((iso_color, iso_mag)))\n",
    "    distances, _ = tree.query(np.column_stack((interp_color, interp_G0)))\n",
    "    mae = np.mean(np.abs(distances))\n",
    "\n",
    "    fit_results.append({\n",
    "        \"MH\": iso[\"MH\"].values[0],\n",
    "        \"logAge\": iso[\"logAge\"].values[0],\n",
    "        \"age\": 10 ** iso[\"logAge\"].values[0],\n",
    "        \"MAE\": mae,\n",
    "        \"iso_color\": iso_color,\n",
    "        \"iso_mag\": iso_mag,\n",
    "        \"file_path\": path\n",
    "    })\n",
    "\n",
    "# ========== Select Best-Fit Isochrone ==========\n",
    "best_fit = min(fit_results, key=lambda x: x[\"MAE\"])\n",
    "iso_color = best_fit[\"iso_color\"]\n",
    "iso_mag = best_fit[\"iso_mag\"]\n",
    "\n",
    "# ========== Select Extra-Tidal Stars Within ±0.1 mag ==========\n",
    "extra_selected = []\n",
    "\n",
    "for _, star in extra_df.iterrows():\n",
    "    color_diff = np.abs(iso_color - star[\"bp_rp_0\"])\n",
    "    mag_diff = np.abs(iso_mag - star[\"G0\"])\n",
    "    match = np.any((color_diff <= color_tol) & (mag_diff <= mag_tol))\n",
    "    if match:\n",
    "        extra_selected.append(star)\n",
    "\n",
    "extra_selected_df = pd.DataFrame(extra_selected)\n",
    "print(f\"\\nFinal count of extra-tidal stars within ±0.1 mag of best-fit isochrone: {len(extra_selected_df)}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# ========== Output Best-Fit Info ==========\n",
    "print(\"\\nBest-Fit Isochrone:\")\n",
    "print(f\"File     : {best_fit['file_path']}\")\n",
    "print(f\"[Fe/H]   : {best_fit['MH']:.2f}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Age      : {best_fit['age']:.2e} yr\")\n",
    "print(f\"MAE      : {best_fit['MAE']:.4f}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# ========== Plot CMD ==========\n",
    "plt.figure(figsize=(6, 6))\n",
    "plt.scatter(cluster_df[\"bp_rp_0\"], cluster_df[\"G0\"], s=5, color='blue', alpha=0.5, label=\"Cluster CMD\")\n",
    "plt.scatter(extra_df[\"bp_rp_0\"], extra_df[\"G0\"], s=5, color='green', alpha=0.4, label=\"Extra-Tidal Candidates\")\n",
    "plt.scatter(extra_selected_df[\"bp_rp_0\"], extra_selected_df[\"G0\"], s=8, color='red', label=\"±0.1 mag from Isochrone\")\n",
    "plt.scatter(iso_color, iso_mag, color='black', s=10,\n",
    "            label=f\"Best Isochrone\\n[Fe/H]={best_fit['MH']:.2f}, Age={best_fit['age']:.1e} yr\")\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.gca().invert_yaxis()\n",
    "plt.xlabel(r\"$(G_{BP} - G_{RP})_0$\")\n",
    "plt.ylabel(r\"$G_0$ (Extinction-corrected)\")\n",
    "plt.title(f\"Isochrone Fitting (DM = {fixed_DM})\")\n",
    "plt.legend()\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()\n"
   ]
  },
